.\"
.\" SEMCTL(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH SEMCTL 2 "2026-06-07" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
semctl \- System V semaphore control operations
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library
.RI ( libc ", " \-lc )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/sem.h>
.PP
.BI "int semctl(int " semid ", int " semnum ", int " cmd ", ... /* union semun " arg " */);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR semctl ()
performs the control operation
.I cmd
on the System V semaphore set identified by
.IR semid ,
or on the
.IR semnum -th
semaphore of that set.  Operations that need a fourth argument take a
.IR "union semun" :
.PP
.in +4n
.nf
union semun {
    int              val;    /* SETVAL */
    struct semid_ds *buf;    /* IPC_STAT, IPC_SET */
    unsigned short  *array;  /* GETALL, SETALL */
};
.fi
.in
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B IPC_STAT
Copy the
.I semid_ds
of the set into
.IR arg.buf .
.TP
.B IPC_SET
Set the owner uid/gid and permission mode of the set from
.IR arg.buf .
.TP
.B IPC_RMID
Remove the set immediately; any process blocked in
.BR semop (2)
on it is woken with
.BR EIDRM .
.TP
.B GETVAL
Return the value of semaphore
.IR semnum .
.TP
.B SETVAL
Set the value of semaphore
.I semnum
to
.IR arg.val .
.TP
.B GETALL
Store all semaphore values into
.IR arg.array .
.TP
.B SETALL
Set all semaphore values from
.IR arg.array .
.TP
.B GETPID
Return the pid of the process that last operated on semaphore
.IR semnum .
.TP
.B GETNCNT
Return the number of processes waiting for semaphore
.I semnum
to increase.
.TP
.B GETZCNT
Return the number of processes waiting for semaphore
.I semnum
to become zero.
.SH RETURN VALUE
For
.BR GETVAL ,
.BR GETPID ,
.BR GETNCNT ,
and
.B GETZCNT
the requested value is returned.  Other commands return 0 on success.
On error \-1 is returned and
.I errno
is set.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EACCES
The caller lacks the permission required for
.IR cmd .
.TP
.B EFAULT
The address pointed to by
.I arg
is inaccessible.
.TP
.B EIDRM
The set was removed.
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I semid
or
.I cmd
is invalid, or
.I semnum
is out of range.
.TP
.B EPERM
.B IPC_SET
or
.B IPC_RMID
was requested by a process that is neither the owner/creator nor
privileged.
.TP
.B ERANGE
.B SETVAL
or
.B SETALL
specified a value greater than
.BR SEMVMX .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR semget (2),
.BR semop (2)
